slug: content-format-check
version: 1.0.0
status: active
created: 2026-05-04
origin: >
  User observed extra spaces in ClawCamp Substack essay draft and requested
  objective codification for multi-platform format enforcement before publishing.
description: >
  Platform-aware content formatting validator. Catches double spaces, trailing
  whitespace, excess blank lines, and platform-specific violations (LinkedIn URL
  suppression, Twitter character limits, Instagram link limitations, etc.).
  Python-based for unicode safety and special-char portability.
enforcement:
  how: HOW.sh
  audit: AUDIT.sh
  watch: WATCH.sh
  check_engine: check.py
  log: ~/.cyborg-enforcement-log.jsonl
platforms:
  - substack
  - linkedin
  - twitter
  - reddit
  - instagram
  - universal (no platform specified)
applies_to:
  - any content before publishing to a distribution surface
  - essays, posts, threads, captions, comments
  - campaign masters before spoke deployment
litmus: >
  Run HOW.sh with text + platform before attaching content to any publishing surface.
  Exit 0 = ship. Exit 1 = BLOCK (must fix). Exit 2 = WARN (review before ship).
dispatch_slug: content-format-check
